|------|-------------|-----|
| Validation | Throws `IllegalArgumentException` on null/empty | Required by spec |
| Record Type lookup | Queries `RecordType` by `DeveloperName = 'Household'` | Avoids hard-coded Ids; works across orgs |
| Account insert | Creates an Account with only the `RecordTypeId` set | NPSP's trigger/flow detects the Household RT and auto-generates the name and greeting from the primary contact |
| Contact insert | Sets `AccountId` on every contact, then inserts them in one bulk DML | Single DML for performance; all contacts land in the same household |
| Primary contact update | Sets `Primary_Contact__c` to `members[0].Id` | Explicitly designates the first contact as primary, which drives NPSP's naming convention |

Because everything happens in a single Apex transaction, any failure (e.g. a validation rule on Contact) rolls back the Account as well, guaranteeing no orphaned or empty households are left behind.

